        "summary": "`run --json` now works: it prints a compact JSON receipt instead of replaying the captured output. The required visible check passes. The full suite ran 60 tests: all `test_confidence.py` and new receipt tests passed, and the 5 failures are all diagnostics tests not caused by this change.\n\n**Change** (`skills/confidence-protocol/scripts/confidence.py`):\n- Added the `--json` flag to `run`.\n- The runner now fingerprints the workspace before the child starts and saves that as `workspace_start` in the run record. The existing end-of-run fingerprint stays in `workspace`, so current stale-workspace validation is unchanged.\n- With `--json`, the captured log is still fully read and its SHA256 recorded; it just isn't replayed. After the record is published, one line of JSON is printed: `id`, `exit_code` (signed child status), `termination_reason`, `record` (`runs/<id>.json`) and `log` (`runs/<id>.log`). Both paths are relative to the evidence directory. It also includes `workspace_binding`.\n- `workspace_binding` is `unknown` if either fingerprint is missing (e.g. not a Git repo), `unchanged` only if the root and hash are the same before and after, and `changed` otherwise. So a source mutation can never show as `unchanged`.\n- Without `--json`, output replay and the CLI exit code are unchanged. A signal exit is still stored as a negative number in the record and receipt, and the CLI returns 128+N.\n\n**Proof map:**\n- **R1 \u2013 compact receipt:** passed. The receipt is under 1 KB, has the right fields, and its paths match the record.\n- **R2 \u2013 full binary output and hash:** passed. A 128 KiB+ output with `\\xff\\x00` bytes was stored byte-for-byte and its SHA256 matches.\n- **R3 \u2013 default replay unchanged:** passed (`test_run_captures_success_and_returns_child_status` and the new default-replay test).\n- **R4 \u2013 failure status kept:** passed. Exit 7, child exit 125, SIGTERM (-15 in receipt/record, 143 from the CLI), timeout 124 with its reason, and a failed launch (125, no stdout, no record) all behave correctly. The visible check `test_run_records_failure_and_returns_child_status` passes.\n- **R5 \u2013 mutation shows `changed`:** passed, including a mutation combined with a failing exit (3). A non-Git directory shows `unknown`.\n\nThese were checked by a new test file, `skills/confidence-protocol/tests/test_run_receipt.py`, adapted from `.protocol/tests/test_run_receipt.py`. I dropped its `version == 2` assertion because version-2 records belong to an excluded part of PR45.\n\n**About the 5 diagnostics failures:** the sandbox sets `CONFIDENCE_DISABLE_DIAGNOSTICS=1`, which turns off telemetry. With that variable unset, only `test_doctor_reports_required_health_checks` fails, and it fails the same way on an untouched copy of HEAD (extracted with `git archive`) in this sandbox.\n\n**Excluded (outside the receipt slice by the task statement):** version-2 records and `capture_sha256`, `git-content-v1` binding, interruption and publication recovery, and doc/changelog edits.\n\n**Limits and rollback:**\n- Validation still accepts a supporting run whose source changed during the run, as long as the tree matches its end state. The receipt and record now show that change but don't block it.\n- The fingerprint doesn't cover ignored files or a change made and then undone during the run.\n- To roll back, revert `confidence.py` and delete the new test file.",
